### Worktrees.

# The changes counted in another worktree are of its tracked files alone.
worktrees-tracked-only = Counts changes to tracked files; untracked files are not looked for

## The menu entries of a worktree.

# Adds a worktree at a branch or a commit.
worktrees-new-here = New worktree here…
worktrees-new = New worktree…
# $name is the name of the worktree's folder.
worktrees-open-named = Open worktree { $name }
worktrees-open-here = Open here, in place of this tab
worktrees-open-in-tab = Open in a new tab
worktrees-remove = Remove…
# $why is one of the reasons below.
worktrees-remove-not = Remove ({ $why })
worktrees-remove-with-branch = Remove with its branch…
worktrees-unlock = Unlock
worktrees-lock = Lock…
worktrees-lock-main = Lock (it is the main one)
worktrees-terminal = Open a terminal there
worktrees-move = Move…
# $why is one of the reasons below.
worktrees-move-not = Move ({ $why })
worktrees-prune = Forget worktrees that are gone
# All the menu of a worktree whose folder is being deleted says.
worktrees-being-removed = Being removed…

## Why a worktree cannot be removed or moved.

worktrees-why-main = it is the main one
worktrees-why-locked = it is locked
